.Dd October 4, 2026
.Dt DESKTOP-SCREENSHOT 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm desktop-screenshot ,
.Nm greeter-screenshot
.Nd grab each monitor to a PNG
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl Fl feedback
.Op Fl Fl greeter
.Nm greeter-screenshot
.Op Fl Fl feedback
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
grabs each connected monitor with
.Xr ffmpeg 1
.Cm x11grab
and writes a PNG.
One connected monitor produces one file.
More than one produces one file per monitor, named with the monitor
after the timestamp.
The pointer is not drawn.
.Pp
One monitor writes
.Pa ~/screenshot- Ns Ar YYYY.MM.DD-HH.MM.SS Ns Pa .png .
More than one writes
.Pa ~/screenshot- Ns Ar YYYY.MM.DD-HH.MM.SS Ns Pa - Ns Ar monitor Ns Pa .png ,
the monitor name after the timestamp.
.Pa ~/screenshot-latest.png
is a symbolic link to the newest grab.
The name
.Nm greeter-screenshot ,
or
.Fl Fl greeter ,
writes the same names under
.Pa /tmp
and makes them mode 0644.
.Pp
With no options the grab is quiet.
.Fl Fl feedback
shows the file name through
.Xr bosd 1 ,
a green caption.
.Sh ENVIRONMENT
.Bl -tag -width "DISPLAY"
.It Ev DISPLAY
X server.
The default is
.Pa :0 .
.It Ev HOME
Directory of a session grab.
.El
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width "~/screenshot-YYYY.MM.DD-HH.MM.SS.png"
.It Pa ~/screenshot-YYYY.MM.DD-HH.MM.SS.png
Session grab.
One file when a single monitor is connected.
.It Pa ~/screenshot-YYYY.MM.DD-HH.MM.SS- Ns Ar monitor Ns Pa .png
One file per monitor when more than one is connected.
.It Pa ~/screenshot-latest.png
Link to the newest session grab.
.It Pa /tmp/screenshot-YYYY.MM.DD-HH.MM.SS.png
Greeter grab.
.It Pa /tmp/screenshot-latest.png
Link to the newest greeter grab.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Nm
exits 0 when the PNG is written.
It exits 1 when the grab fails.
A bad argument exits 2.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr bhotkeys 1 ,
.Xr bosd 1 ,
.Xr ffmpeg 1 ,
.Xr window-screenshot 1 ,
.Xr xrandr 1
.Sh AUTHORS
.An Devin Teske Aq Mt dteske@FreeBSD.org
